From aa6c5fdbb7924705f8bc67b4a325260cfe11741d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lior Ben Ishay <liorbi@maxlinear.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 09:34:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-101523 Add MRU TX Power enable commands

Issue:
The current implementation lacks support for managing MRU TX power settings, which may affect performance in specific scenarios.

Fix:
Added two new vendor command identifiers for MRU TX power management in `vendor_cmds_copy.h`:
- `LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_SET_MRU_TX_POWER_ENABLE`
- `LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_GET_MRU_TX_POWER_ENABLE`

Test:
- Dry-Run sanity test
- GCI

AI code review:
Yes

Impact analysis:
This change introduces new command identifiers, which may increase the complexity of command handling but should not introduce regressions if properly managed.
---
 src/common/vendor_cmds_copy.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/common/vendor_cmds_copy.h b/src/common/vendor_cmds_copy.h
index 61cdd23c1..dcbcd9a92 100644
--- a/src/common/vendor_cmds_copy.h
+++ b/src/common/vendor_cmds_copy.h
@@ -422,6 +422,8 @@ enum ltq_nl80211_vendor_subcmds {
   LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_SET_PCIE_AUTO_GEN_ENABLE,
   LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_SET_VW_TEST_MODE,
   LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_GET_VW_TEST_MODE,
+  LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_SET_MRU_TX_POWER_ENABLE,
+  LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_GET_MRU_TX_POWER_ENABLE,
   LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_SET_PBAC,
   LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_SET_AQM_STA_EN,
   LTQ_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_GET_AQM_STA_EN,
-- 
